s:`What TeddyCloud does`,featuresHint:`Features and the running version`,featuresIntro:`TeddyCloud is your own server for your Tonieboxes: content, settings and updates come from you instead of the tonie cloud.`,featContent:`Content for the boxes`,featContent1:`Pass original content through and cache it`,featContent2:`Own content from the library, playlists too`,featContent3:`Web radio and streams, converted live with ffmpeg`,featContent4:`Live content that always starts from the beginning`,featContent5:`Replace the box's system sounds`,featContent6:`Keep unknown tags instead of deleting them`,featTonies:`Tonies`,featTonies1:`Content, figure, live and cloud for each tag`,featTonies2:`Search, filter, sort, export, change several at once`,featTonies3:`Listen in the browser, download as OGG`,featTonies4:`Custom models with picture, title and chapter names`,featTonies5:`Print labels with TeddyStudio`,featLibrary:`Library`,featLibrary1:`Upload audio files and turn them into tonie files, in the browser or on the server`,featLibrary2:`Build playlists, split tonie files into chapters`,featLibrary3:`Folders, move, rename, mark as heard`,featLibrary4:`Share with other users`,featBoxes:`Boxes`,featBoxes1:`Up to 16 boxes, each with its own settings`,featBoxes2:`Volume limits, LED, slapping and cloud access`,featBoxes3:`With the custom firmware: remote control, profiles, event tags, updates`,featBoxes4:`Box log (RTNL) live`,featSetup:`Box setup`,featSetup1:`Tell the box's chip by its MAC address`,featSetup2:`CC3200 and CC3235 with a guide, patches in the browser`,featSetup3:`Read, patch and flash an ESP32 in the browser`,featMore:`More`,featMore1:`Users, groups and rights, two-factor login`,featMore2:`Home Assistant via MQTT`,featMore3:`Plugins for the web interface`,featMore4:`As an app on the phone, light, dark or matrix`,changes:`Changes`,changesHint:`What changed in this web interface`,changesIntro:`The changes of web2, newest first`,translations:`Translations`,translationsIntro:`German and English are complete; the other languages show what is still missing in English.`,translationsTexts:`Texts of the app`,translationsSettings:`Names of the settings`,translationsSettingsHint:`Where a name is missing, the server's English one shows.`,translationsHint:`How complete each language is`,credits:`Credits and legal`,creditsHint:`What web2 took from others`,creditsOpenBox:`Guide "open the box": after the iFixit guides by Tobias Isakeit`,creditsFonts:`Fonts in TeddyStudio: Google Fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1`,creditsFlags:`Flags: country-flag-icons by Nikolay Kuchumov`,creditsIcons:`Icons: Lucide`,creditsLogo:`Logo: Flaticon`,creditsClassic:`teddyCloud's classic web interface, where pictures, the ESP32 flasher and texts come from`,legal:`Legal`,legalText:`Toniebox, Tonie and tonies are trademarks of tonies GmbH (formerly Boxine GmbH). This project is not affiliated with tonies GmbH. Changing the firmware, opening the box or using its debug port is at your own risk. The software comes without any warranty (GPL 3.0).`,meeting:`Tonie meeting`,meetingText:`{{n}} tonies have come`,toniesWithoutAudioId:`Tonies without audio ID`,communityIntro:`Be part of the community: write code, comment on issues or join the talk on Telegram.`,getInvolved:`Get involved`,communityTelegram:`The first place for help and for everyone who wants to work on teddyCloud.`,communityForum:`The knowledge base: ask questions whose answers help others too.`,communityWiki:`Installing teddyCloud and solutions for common problems.`,communityGithub:`All sources: fork repositories, contribute features, report issues.`,faqTitle:`FAQ`,faqQ1:`How do I make a tonie fetch new content?`,faqA1:`Press one ear of the box for about 3 seconds until a sound plays (freshness check). A second sound confirms it is done.`,faqQ2:`How do I make a file with several chapters?`,faqA2:`Choose up to 99 audio files under "Upload"; every file becomes a chapter.`,faqQ3:`How many boxes can one teddyCloud serve?`,faqA3:`Up to 16 Tonieboxes.`,faqQ4:`How does a new tag get into teddyCloud?`,faqA4:`Put it on a connected box; it then shows up under Tonies. With many unknown tags, the filter for the last played ones helps.`,faqQ5:`How do I remove a tag?`,faqA5:`Easiest is to hide it; it stays hidden until it is put on a box again. For good: delete its folder on the SD card of every box and in the content folder.`,faqQ6:`How does a tag get different content on different boxes?`,faqA6:`Give each box its own content folder in its settings. Boxes with the same folder share the content.`,faqQ7:`Why are no tonies shown after a new content folder?`,faqA7:`Do a freshness check on the box: all tags that were ever on it come back. Original tonies have to be put on once so their content is loaded.`,faqQ8:`Why does my own content always start from the beginning?`,faqA8:`"nocloud" has to be on for the tag, and no other tag may have been on the box in between.`,faqQ9:`Why is content not stored in teddyCloud?`,faqA9:`Switch on the settings "Cache Content" and "Dump rUID/auth"; "Cache to library" is recommended too.`,faqQ10:`Why does my RFID tag not work?`,faqA10:`Only NXP SLIX-L tags work (the CC3200 box can enable others, see the wiki). Keep 2–3 mm between the tag and the box.`,supportTitle:`A good support request`,supportIntro:`So you get help quickly (English is best):`,support1:`Describe the problem in one sentence.`,support2:`Step by step: what you did, what you expected, what happened.`,support3:`Name the versions: teddyCloud (System), box model and firmware, browser.`,support4:`Attach the log of teddyCloud, for box problems the box log too.`,support5:`Screenshots often show more than words.`,support6:`What you already tried, so nobody suggests it again.`,contributeToniesJson:`Missing data in tonies.json`,contributeToniesJsonHint:`These tonies lack their audio IDs. If you have one of them, help to add the data (e.g. with TeddyBench).`,contributors:`Contributors`,contributo